 "summary": "The new public surface is minimal and alias-free: every HalfLine.lean lemma is either consumed in Strip.lean or a standalone upstream-style fact, and the three private helpers in Strip.lean are one-step specialisations of already-public API to the Mellin bridge's data, not general infrastructure. The characteristic API for mellinDis/MellinDisConvergent is complete (both _def lemmas now (rfl)/(Iff.rfl), weighted-space iff, Re-only form, monotonicity with upper-set and ordConnected, both mellin bridges) and correctly annotated.",
